Hazard the gate cannot see: reviewers reuse the same scratchpad names across runs. Examples: rv89 (3 runs), probe (5), sync (4), syncchk (4), sc (3), fx, p, rc, rev89, rv, kb, i42.md, syncsim, synccheck. A run that `rm -rf`s and recreates such a folder while a sibling uses it can have its content swapped mid-run, and the run still "wrote it first". The new .scratch/work/ sentence is the fix for runs launched from now on.

